            "finding": "\"`sendReturnConfirmation`\" addresses the mail to \"`order.id`\" instead of \"`order.customer.email`\", so \"`queueMail`\" always rejects the recipient and the error is only logged; no return confirmation is ever sent."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/admin.ts:42-48",
            "finding": "\"`adminRefund`\" still limits the refund with \"`refundedTotal`\", which now counts only settled refunds, and then calls the unchecked \"`issueRefund`\"; pending cash refunds are ignored, so a goodwill refund can push the order past its total, against the README rule that refunds never exceed what was paid. It should go through \"`requestRefund`\" / \"`refundable`\"."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "ROBUSTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/credit.ts:47-54",
            "finding": "\"`spendCredit`\" reads \"`balance`\" before \"`await book(...)`\" and writes \"`balance - amount`\" afterwards; the comment says booking is asynchronous, so two concurrent spends both pass the check (double spending), and a grant made during the wait is overwritten (lost update)."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/returns.ts:68-74",
            "finding": "Each line's share is rounded separately with \"`Math.round`\", so the shares of all lines need not add up to \"`order.total`\" (e.g. subtotal 1500, total 1250, three items of 500 give 3 x 417 = 1251). The customer is then paid too little, or the last return is rejected as exceeding what is left, which breaks the README promise that returning everything pays back exactly what was paid."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:38-40",
            "finding": "\"`isRepeat`\" still compares only \"`order.status === event.status`\". After a partial refund the order is \"`partially_refunded`\", so a redelivered \"`refunded`\" event makes \"`settleRefund`\" throw \"already settled\" and a redelivered \"`paid`\" event makes \"`markPaid`\" throw. The provider keeps retrying instead of getting the acknowledgement the comment promises."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/report.ts:14",
            "finding": "\"`revenue`\" counts only \"`status === \"paid\"`\", so an order drops out of the daily report's revenue completely once it becomes \"`partially_refunded`\", even though most of its total was kept; the new status was not taken into account here."
        }
    ]
}
